    "kind": "issue",
    "title": "New user: Profile page 404, git push fails",
    "body": "I just created my account and created a repo. However, I found that my profile page 404, although it's accessible via did:\n\n- [Profile page (404)](https://tangled.org/superkenvery.tngl.sh)\n- [Profile via did (normal)](https://tangled.org/did:plc:cnx5rmsyvousaqjfbbzzllbi?tab=overview)\n\nWhat's more, I can't push to the repo, even though I (think I) correctly configured the ssh keys:\n\n```\ngit push -u tangle HEAD\nEnumerating objects: 170, done.\nknot: couldn't read the account records needed to check your ssh key, retry shortly\nsend-pack: unexpected disconnect while reading sideband packet\nCounting objects: 100% (170/170), done.\nDelta compression using up to 8 threads\nCompressing objects: 100% (154/154), done.\nfatal: the remote end hung up unexpectedly\n```\n\n(But I successfully pushed as of writing this. Profile page is still 404 though)",
